<section class="section section-soft" id="my-story"><div class="shell story-editorial">
  <div class="story-title"><p class="section-index">03 / How I got here</p><h2 class="section-title">I built an agency.<br>Then I chose to stop.</h2></div>
  <div class="story-excerpt"><p>I started Upstack Studio in 2017. My team and I spent years building web and mobile software with business owners.</p><p>That work taught me to look past the list of features. What does the customer need? What will the team actually use? Is this the right problem to spend money on?</p><p>Eventually, I had a different question to answer: was this still the business I wanted to build?</p><p>The answer was no. I shut the agency down and chose a different path.</p><p class="story-turn">You can be good at building something and still decide it isn’t where your next few years should go.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">Read the full story</a></div>
  <figure class="story-wide"><img src="/assets/images/adrian/upstack-team.webp" alt="Adrian Ching with the Upstack Studio team" width="1130" height="1130" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><figcaption>The Upstack Studio chapter. The work still shapes how I think.</figcaption></figure>
</div></section>

